{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>Blessed be Avram of El Elyon, who possesses heaven and earth.</b> Above (Genesis 14:18) it says 'and he was priest of El Elyon,' and he did not mention 'who possesses heaven and earth,' because before Avram came, the Holy One, blessed be He, was called 'El Elyon,' for His kingdom, blessed be He, was not recognized among those below — as Rashi explained on the verse 'HaShem, Elohim of the heavens, who took me from my father's house' (Genesis 24:7). And Avram acquired heaven and earth for HaShem, for he publicized to all His existence, blessed be He, among those below; therefore he always mentioned 'who possesses heaven and earth' in connection with Avram. Another matter: since all blessings come from the dew of the heavens and from the fatness of the earth, therefore he mentioned 'who possesses heaven and earth' in connection with the blessing. And likewise when he said below (Genesis 14:22) 'I have lifted up my hand to HaShem, El Elyon, who possesses heaven and earth, if from a thread to a sandal-strap,' etc. — he said this because the Holy One, blessed be He, is able to give him from His own, from the chief produce of the heavens above and from the deep couching beneath; therefore I will take nothing of yours.'" "<b>And some say, that which he said — 'and you shall not say, I have made Avram rich.'</b> Its meaning is not 'so that you shall not say,' but rather he actually said: I know of you that you will not say 'I have made Avram rich,' and even so, it is not my wish to take anything. Another matter: at first He was Elyon, for they said that His providence, blessed be He, does not extend below the sphere of the moon; and through this war they saw eye to eye that He is also Elohim of the earth and His providence is also among those below, for not by strength does a man prevail but only through His providence, blessed be He."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:28:15.790448793Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}